! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F209D "TESTS OF
! INDICATORS" for ADD DOUBLE TO MAGNITUDE, sub-tests D1-D5
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf pp.106-107, octal
! 015614.40-015652.00, where F209D6 begins): the four arithmetic
! result indicators -- RLZ, RZ, RGZ and RN.
!
! Each sub-test runs one D+MG and then asks after every indicator in
! turn, one SIC/branch pair per question, the branch going to the
! error halt when the answer is wrong:
!
!   D1  RLZ and RN on   DLN accumulator (FPK31 with FPK37's fraction
!                       in its low half) + FPK39
!   D2  RLZ and RN on   DLN FPK37 + FPK38, low half left zero
!   D3  RZ on           an all-ones right half from C1111, then DL(U)
!                       FPK0 + D+MG(U) FPK0 -- a zero result
!   D4  RGZ on          DL(U) FPK31 + FPK32
!   D5  RGZ on          DL(U) FPK37 + FPK38
!
! D1 and D2 are the ones that bear on the model. Their accumulators
! are loaded NEGATIVE with DLN, and D+MG assumes the accumulator
! positive for the addition -- so a result whose indicators were fed
! the addition's sign would read RGZ, not RLZ and RN. The sign has to
! be restored BEFORE the indicators are set, not merely before the
! sign byte is written. That ordering is what these two check.
!
! Transcribed as printed: D1's third question is BRGZ where its
! comment says "error if RZ on", and D2 asks the same question with
! BRZ. The encodings are unambiguous -- 1304.35 42 against
! 1304.34 C2 -- so this is the listing's own inconsistency, not a
! transcription slip. D1 therefore asks about RGZ twice and never
! about RZ.
!
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.176. D6-D9, the Lost Significance half, are not transcribed
! here; PASS sits exactly where D6 begins.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), DLN(U), C0011 into the accumulator at offset
! 20, C1111, D+MG(U), SIC, and the eight indicator branches
! BZRLZ/BRLZ, BZRZ/BRZ, BZRGZ/BRGZ, BZRN/BRN.
! verify_fp_arith_f209d1_5_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: all five passed on the first run, and D1 pins an ordering
! that nothing before it could. Restoring the accumulator's sign only
! where the sign BYTE is written -- so the byte comes out right but
! the result indicators are fed the addition's sign -- leaves F209C
! passing and halts at D1's first question, BZRLZ (SIC stores
! 015620.00). F209C checks all eight sign byte bits and still cannot
! see this, because the byte is correct; only an indicator test can.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --

        SLC, (8)22005.0
FPK0    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)22044.0
FPK31   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031000000000000000000
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22052.0
FPK37   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525240
FPK38   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031052525252525252520
FPK39   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001052525252525252520

! The listing prints NO label at this address -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand. The listing's own FADM4 is at 015672.00, on
! F209E1; FADM2 (015365.40) and FADM3 (015576.40) are real and are used
! at their real addresses in the F209B and F209C programs.
!
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)15614.40
ENTRY   B, $+.32                 ! F209D1: RLZ and RN on
        DLN(U), FPK31            ! L12-59 +0, LR60-107 unequal to 0
        C0011(BU,48), FPK37+.12, 20
        D+MG(U), FPK39
        SIC, SEN
        BZRLZ, SERS              ! error if RLZ off
        SIC, SEN
        BZRN, SERS               ! error if RN off
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS               ! listing's comment says "error if RZ on"
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32                 ! F209D2: RLZ and RN on
        DLN(U), FPK37            ! L12-59 unequal to 0, LR60-107 +0
        D+MG(U), FPK38
        SIC, SEN
        BZRLZ, SERS              ! error if RLZ indicator off
        SIC, SEN
        BZRN, SERS               ! error if RN indicator off
        SIC, SEN
        BRZ, SERS                ! error if RZ indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32                 ! F209D3: RZ indicator on
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1       ! R44-63 unequal to 0
        DL(U), FPK0              ! L12-59 +0, LR60-107 +0
        D+MG(U), FPK0
        SIC, SEN
        BZRZ, SERS               ! error if RZ indicator off
        SIC, SEN
        BRLZ, SERS               ! error if RLZ indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRN, SERS                ! error if RN indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        B, $+.32                 ! F209D4: RGZ indicator on
        DL(U), FPK31             ! L12-59 +0, LR60-107 unequal to 0
        D+MG(U), FPK32
        SIC, SEN
        BZRGZ, SERS              ! error if RGZ indicator off
        SIC, SEN
        BRLZ, SERS               ! error if RLZ indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRN, SERS                ! error if RN indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRZ, SERS                ! error if RZ indicator on
        B, $+.32                 ! F209D5: RGZ indicator on
        DL(U), FPK37             ! L12-59 unequal to 0, LR60-107 +0
        D+MG(U), FPK38
        SIC, SEN
        BZRGZ, SERS              ! error if RGZ indicator off
        SIC, SEN
        BRLZ, SERS               ! error if RLZ indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRN, SERS                ! error if RN indicator on
        SIC, SEN
        BRZ, SERS                ! error if RZ indicator on
PASS    BEW, $                   ! 015652.00: where F209D6 begins
        END, ENTRY
